  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "I set my alarm for 7:00 AM, and every night I convince myself I'm actually getting up at 7:00 AM. Then morning hits, the alarm goes off, loud, annoying, and without even opening my eyes, I hit the snooze button like it's instinct. I tell myself, \"Five more minutes, that's it.\" But those five minutes always turn into 10, then 15, and next thing I know, I'm lying there doing the math, figuring out what I can skip to still make it on time. There's always this one moment where I'm awake enough to get up, but I just don't move. I'm staring at the ceiling thinking, \"Yeah, not yet.\" And every single morning, I swear I'm going to quit the snooze habit. I'll wake up the first time, be disciplined, start fresh, all that. But then the next day comes around and yeah, same alarm, same snooze, same negotiation with myself. Honestly, the snooze button should come with a warning label, something like, \"Use once, regret all day.\"",
      "start_time": 0.119,
      "end_time": 60.34,
